> specs\aqa\drama-8261-8261.md:5053:6.7 Access to assessment: diversity and inclusion
  specs\aqa\drama-8261-8261.md:5054:General qualifications are designed to prepare students for a wide range of 
occupations and
  specs\aqa\drama-8261-8261.md:5055:further study. Therefore our qualifications must assess a wide range of 
competences.
  specs\aqa\drama-8261-8261.md:5056:
  specs\aqa\drama-8261-8261.md:5068:6.7.1 Students with disabilities and special needs
  specs\aqa\drama-8261-8261.md:5069:
  specs\aqa\drama-8261-8261.md:5070:We can make arrangements for disabled students and students with special needs to 
help them
> specs\aqa\drama-8261-8261.md:5071:access the assessments, as long as the competences being tested are not changed. 
Access
> specs\aqa\drama-8261-8261.md:5072:arrangements must be agreed before the assessment. For example, a Braille paper 
would be a
  specs\aqa\drama-8261-8261.md:5073:reasonable adjustment for a Braille reader but not for a student who does not read 
Braille.
  specs\aqa\drama-8261-8261.md:5074:
  specs\aqa\drama-8261-8261.md:5075:We are required by the Equality Act 2010 to make reasonable adjustments to remove 
or lessen
  specs\aqa\drama-8261-8261.md:5085:6.7.2 Special consideration
  specs\aqa\drama-8261-8261.md:5086:
  specs\aqa\drama-8261-8261.md:5087:We can give special consideration to students who have been disadvantaged at the 
time of the
> specs\aqa\drama-8261-8261.md:5088:assessment through no fault of their own – for example a temporary illness, injury 
or serious
> specs\aqa\drama-8261-8261.md:5089:problem such as the death of a relative. We can only do this after the assessment.
  specs\aqa\drama-8261-8261.md:5090:
  specs\aqa\drama-8261-8261.md:5091:Your exams officer should apply online for special consideration at aqa.org.uk/eaqa
