scripts\_retrofc\units\drama-aqa__romeo-and-juliet\raw\L08.txt:54:  <p>Exam answers on practitioners fail when they 
describe the practitioner&rsquo;s biography without applying the technique to a specific moment of the play. The 
question is always: what would a director drawing on this practitioner DO differently at this named moment? A good 
answer names the technique, explains what the director would do and names the effect on the audience &mdash; all 
three, in sequence.</p>



