+    "field": "exam_tip_html",
+    "find": "<p data-narration-id=\"n16\">The most common error on design questions is describing a &lsquo;mood&rsquo; without naming specific elements. Writing &ldquo;I would use romantic lighting&rdquo; is worth very little. A strong answer names the lantern type (profile, Fresnel, birdie, flood), the colour (a specific gel colour or temperature &mdash; warm amber, cold blue-white, daylight neutral), the direction (from above, from the side, from front-of-house) and the effect on the audience at a named moment. The same applies to costume: name the fabric (brocade, cotton, leather), the colour, the silhouette and the symbolic meaning. For the 8-mark designer question, you are expected to make specific choices for one or two design disciplines, not give a general overview of the whole production. For the 20-mark response, cover all four departments but ensure each choice is concrete and justified, not merely decorative.</p>",
